    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "method",
      "heading": "Method",
      "chunks": [
        {
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c01",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c1_method_two_parts_kill_finite_nudge",
          "text": "The method has two parts. To kill the finite-nudge bias, the authors build on holomorphic EP: they drive the network with an oscillating teaching signal and use a Cauchy integral from complex analysis to recover the exact error vector, no matter how large the nudge and even when the Jacobian is asymmetric.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
